TI  - Technique of video-assisted thoracoscopic left pneumonectomy.
PG  - 32
LID - 10.21037/jovs.2017.02.06 [doi]
LID - 32
AB  - Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) approaches to lobectomy for treatment 
      of early stage non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) have generally been accepted to 
      be beneficial. Experience and results for more extensive resections, including 
      thoracoscopic pneumonectomy are limited. Here we report a case with attached 
      videos describing key technical aspects of performing a thoracoscopic left 
      pneumonectomy. This demonstrates the adoption of VATS for tumor pathology 
      requiring pneumonectomy is feasible and can be done safely. Further study is 
      needed to clarify potential advantages or drawbacks to approaching more complex 
      tumor pathology by VATS.
