TI  - Videothoracoscopic Bronchial Sleeve Resection for Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer.
PG  - e13686
LID - 10.7759/cureus.13686 [doi]
LID - e13686
AB  - Nowadays, videothoracoscopic lobectomy is accepted as the standard treatment 
      method in early-stage lung cancer. Sleeve lobectomy, which is an alternative to 
      pneumonectomy in centrally located tumors or peribronchial tumor infiltration, 
      was previously performed via thoracotomy, but it can be performed by 
      video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) in recent years. In this method, 
      without compromising oncological principles, a more comfortable and less morbid 
      postoperative process can be provided to the patient compared to thoracotomy. 
      Here, we aimed the presenting two cases that underwent VATS sleeve lobectomy for 
      non-small cell lung cancer and their results.
