IS  - 1547-4127 (Print)
VI  - 18
IP  - 3
DP  - 2008 Aug
TI  - VATS lobectomy is better than open thoracotomy: what is the evidence for 
      short-term outcomes?
PG  - 249-58
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2008.04.007 [doi]
AB  - VATS lobectomy is an acceptable alternative to open lobectomy for treating 
      early-stage NSCLC. Although no large randomized control trial has compared these 
      procedures, recent large series and case-control studies provide strong evidence 
      that patients undergoing VATS lobectomy have less pain, fewer perioperative 
      complications, shorter chest-tube duration, and decreased length of stay. 
      Increasing evidence supports improved quality of life up to 1 year, less 
      inflammation, and greater safety profile in high-risk patients. More data are 
      needed to better show an improvement in the economic efficacy, ability to more 
      effectively administer adjuvant therapies, and benefit of robotic assistance in 
      VATS lobectomy.
