VI  - 14
IP  - 1
DP  - 2005 Jul
TI  - New therapeutic approaches for early stage non-small cell lung cancer.
PG  - 27-32
AB  - Surgical resection remains the mainstay of therapy for early stage non-small cell 
      lung cancer (NSCLC). Unfortunately, many patients present with advanced stage 
      disease, and many with resectable early stage disease are unable to tolerate 
      pulmonary resection because of compromised cardiopulmonary function. This article 
      reviews the standard and some alternative therapies that are being introduced 
      into clinical practice for early stage NSCLC. New therapies such as sublobar 
      resection with brachytherapy, radiofrequency ablation and stereotactic 
      radiosurgery offer some hope for those patients who are deemed poor candidates 
      for curative resection.
