TI  - [A Review on Comparison of Lobectomy and Segmentectomy in the Treatment of  Early 
      Stage Non-small Cell Lung Cancer].
PG  - 526-531
LID - 10.3779/j.issn.1009-3419.2019.08.08 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is a worldwide malignancy with high morbidity and mortality in the 
      world. With the application of low-dose spiral computed tomography in the 
      screening and diagnosis of lung cancer, more lung cancers are detected at an 
      early stage and cured by surgical treatment. Anatomical lobectomy has long been 
      the standard procedure for the treatment of early stage non-small cell lung 
      cancer. However, whether intentional segmentectomy can be more used remains 
      controversial. And this paper focuses on the question. .
