DP  - 2023 May 25
TI  - Sub-Lobar Resection: The New Standard of Care for Early-Stage Lung Cancer.
LID - 10.3390/cancers15112914 [doi]
LID - 2914
AB  - The Lung Cancer Study Group previously established lobectomy as the standard of 
      care for treatment of clinical T1N0 NSCLC. Advances in imaging technology and 
      refinements in staging have prompted a re-investigation to determine the 
      non-inferiority of sub-lobar resections to lobectomies. Two recent randomized 
      studies, JCOG 0802 and CALGB 140503, are reviewed here in the context of LCSG 
      0821. The studies confirm non-inferiority for sub-lobar resection (wedge or 
      segmentectomy) compared to lobectomy for peripheral T1N0 NSCLC less than or equal 
      to 2 cm. Sub-lobar resection should therefore be considered the new standard of 
      care in this sub-set of patients with NSCLC.
